cost census on main @ 414515c (PR #501 merged) — 2026-08-10/11
==============================================================
Box     Apple M4 Pro, 8P+4E, macOS 26.5.2, aarch64. Idle: foreign_max = 0 on
        331/336 wall rows and 165/165 CPU rows; 1 on 5 wall rows.
Build   cargo --release, default features. No target-cpu=native.
        Ceiling arm = --features probe-untracked, BIT-IDENTICAL to plain
        (CHECKSUM equal on text_q20/c256x2048/ui_q20 at t=8).
        Census arm = --features probe-sites (counts only; its ms/frame is
        perturbed ~3.5x and is NOT used anywhere below).
Locks   every timed run under `measlock`. Builds niced, timed runs never.
Fit     wall and CPU both from a two-point fit total = alpha + beta*frames,
        n_lo/n_hi PER CELL and never past the stream length (4K IVF = 40 or 16
        frames). ROUNDS=8 wall / 5 CPU, rotating arm order, ROUND 1 DISCARDED
        (first touch of each (arm,cell) is cold: ms_lo 283 vs 59-63 on
        ui_q20/plain). Medians; min/max in the wall table.
        CPU = bash `time` keyword user+sys (NOT /usr/bin/time, which shares fd 2
        with the payload on macOS and read 0).
Cross-checks that passed before anything was believed
        * c1024x576 t=8 plain/dav1d = 1.848 vs 1.86 in shard_size_sweep — 0.6%.
        * c1024x576 t=8 tracker CPU / registrations = 6.49 ns vs 6.50 ns in
          SHARD_SIZE_SWEEP.md §5c — 3 digits.
        * loopfilter.rs:833:14 on v4k_8tile t=8 = 3,835,042/frame, the exact
          count OWNERSHIP_MODELS.md §7d option 1 records.
        * ui_q20 t=1 total 189,450/frame = CTX_TL_SPLIT.md §6b's read-side arm.
        * two-point wall fit vs in-process Instant on ui_q20 t=8: 2.544 vs
          2.53-2.57 ms/frame.
        * text_q20 t=8 tracker bucket from the profile = 0.691 CPU ms/frame vs
          plain-untracked = 0.692.
Vectors ~/tmp/ctxtl/{vec,ivf} (content classes, mk_content_classes.sh),
        ~/tmp/shardsize/{vec,ivf} (1:1 crops, mk_shardsize_vectors.sh),
        ~/tmp/rav1d-perf + ~/tmp/recon-yard (v4k_8tile). Every IVF is N repeats
        of the SAME key-frame OBU the AVIF carries, so our arm and dav1d decode
        identical work. Tile geometry parsed per vector (av1_tile_info.py):
        ui/text 1024x576 = 2x1 = 2 TILES; every shardsize crop and v4k_8tile
        = 4x2 = 8 tiles.

